1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Hello everyone, in this session, I will demo how to generate Testcase using GitHub Copilot.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:21,000
To use this feature, first, I need to have Test Workspace Folder created for the item I need to generate Testcase.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
In this session, I will go to Testing Support. Here, I will have two options.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The first option is to create Test Workspace Folder for an item.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
And the second option is to create Test Workspace Folder for a list of other items.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
I will demo the first option first. I will choose One Item here.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Here, I will have three different types of information.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The first information is the database path.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
This is the folder path that contains the database that I have logged from the stream or snapshot.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
The second information is the workspace path.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
I will create a blank folder.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:15,000
And I will take this folder path to contain the outputs in the Tool running process.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The third information is the item name.

15
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
This is the name of the item that I need to create.

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The Test Workspace Folder.

17
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
After I have filled out these three things, I will click on Generate Environment.

18
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:45,000
After completing this step, Tool will show an option to notify.

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
At the same time,

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Visual Studio Code will automatically open and import the test workspace folder of the item you need to create.

21
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Here I will have the source file.

22
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
I will also have two files.

23
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The first is test.cpp and the second is test.h.

25
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Besides, I can use the "Open output" feature.

26
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:27,000
It will help me to open the test workspace folder of the item I need to create.

27
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
For the second option, I will choose List Item.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
I also have three important information.

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
The first is database path.

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The second one is the workspace path.

31
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And the third one is List Items path.

32
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:05,000
I will have an Excel file to store the information of the item name and item path.

33
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
That need to create test workspace folders.

34
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Then I will take the path of this file

35
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:23,000
and enter it into the List Items path field.

36
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Then I will click on "Generate environment".

37
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
After this step is done,

38
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
choose Open output

39
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Then we will see the workspace folder is created

40
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Inside Item list

41
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
After having the test workspace folder for item

42
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
We need to create testcase

43
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
We choose Generate Test Case by A.I. Copilot

44
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Here, I have two fields.

45
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
The first one is the item path

46
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:35,000
I will go to the Test Workspace Folder of an item

47
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
that needs to generate test cases

48
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
For example, this item

49
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:43,000
I will copy the path of this file

50
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:51,000
After that, I will input the first source of information

51
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
And the next one is the database path

52
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Just like the previous step

53
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:05,000
I will also input the data of the folder containing the database

54
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Here, then I will click Auto define object here

55
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:15,000
While the tool is running, we can see the detailed information

58
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:19,000
by clicking on the Show Execution Log here

59
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
There is a Terminal window that will appear

60
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
and will show the detailed information

61
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
while the Tool is running

62
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:47,360
At the end of Auto Define Object, we will go to the next step, which is Prepare Get SUTs.

63
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:11,360
In the pop-up information, we will see that it found 3 SUTs functions and update dropdown.

64
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:18,360
We see that there are 3 functions listed here.

65
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:23,360
We will select one of the 3 functions that we want to generate test case.

66
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,360
In the next step, we will have 2 options.

67
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:31,360
The first option is to generate test case for the function we are selecting here.

68
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:38,360
And the second option is to generate test case for all functions in this item.

69
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:41,360
To make it easier for us to observe the running process,

70
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:46,360
while generating test case, we will open Visual Studio Code

71
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:52,360
And import the test workspace folder of item inside here.

72
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:02,360
So we demonstrate the first option,

73
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:10,360
and generate test case for only one function here, we choose generate one SUT

74
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:16,360
We can see the trigger generate testcase is sent here

75
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:23,360
We will see the information in the Visual Studio Code.

76
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:28,360
We will go to Output and choose GitHub Copilot Chat here.

77
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:33,360
The generate process information will be shown in this terminal.

78
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:39,360
After we see the notification that the test generation is completed,

79
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:44,360
that is, the generate process is done.

80
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:48,360
Next, we will click on Terminal.

81
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:50,360
We will build this test.

82
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:11,360
Here we have 8 Testcases and all 8 Testcases are passed.

83
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:16,360
Next, we will see how the code coverage is.

84
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:20,360
Then we will proceed to build Cantata for this test.

85
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,360
We will click on Build Cantata here.

86
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:57,360
After building Cantata is done,

87
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,360
we will see that in the

88
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:03,360
Test Workspace folder of the item,

89
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:08,360
there is a Cantata folder in the Output folder.

90
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:12,360
We will open Cantata.

91
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,360
Click on Tools.

92
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,360
Then we will go to the C folder.

93
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:21,360
Choose TCC.

94
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:24,360
Go to Tools.

95
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:26,360
Go to Cantata.

96
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:29,360
Then we will open this tool.

97
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:39,360
We will create a project in Cantata.

98
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,360
C Project.

99
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:56,360
We will name the project,

100
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:59,360
like the Item name

101
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:14,360
We will drag the folder Cantata to the new project we've just created in Cantata tool

102
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:26,360
I will click on this .cov file

103
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:30,360
Then I will open this file

104
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:36,360
Here I see that the first function

105
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:39,360
the code color is green

106
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:43,360
This is equivalent to the fact that these lines of code have been covered

107
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:47,360
And these red lines are still not covered

108
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:59,360
Then I will demonstrate my second option

109
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:02,360
is Generate Testcase All SUT

110
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:05,360
Before clicking on this Generate button

111
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:09,360
I will delete the newly created Testcases

112
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,360
In the first option

113
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,360
to avoid being duplicated for the next run time

114
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:30,360
Then I will click on Generate Testcase All SUT here

115
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:34,360
to create Testcases for all functions in this item

116
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:34,360
After finished generating the testcases for 3 functions in this item, I will build the Cantata

117
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:41,360
In this step, we can click on the "Build Cantata" button to build in Tool

118
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:48,360
Or we can build Cantata from the Visual Studio Code

119
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:55,360
I go to Terminal, then select Run Task..., and select "Cantata++ coverage measurement"

120
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:18,360
In the Terminal section, I can see the values and code coverage has reached 100%

121
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:21,360
We will go to Tool Cantata

122
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:27,360
We will see that the code had been covered 100%

123
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:35,360
I will gradually drag the Cantata folder into the project

124
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:38,360
in Cantata tool

125
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:54,860
Here we can see that the line code of these three functions of this item are already covered

126
00:18:54,860 --> 00:19:00,860
And so the color of these changes into green

127
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:17,360
Now we click on Cantata, choose View, choose Report Viewer to view this report

128
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:22,360
We can view the test report here

129
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:32,360
And the coverage that we can see here

130
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:34,360
This is the end of my demonstration

131
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:37,360
Thank you for watching
